    },
    {
      "id": 2,
      "text": "The Lake Harriet Bandshell, built in 1985, sits on the eastern edge and is a fifth‑generation music venue.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        7,
        8
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Linden_Hills%2C_Minneapolis"
    },
    {
      "id": 3,
      "text": "The Como‑Harriet streetcar line, extended in the 1920s, sparked the neighborhood’s commercial corridor along Upton Avenue and 43rd Street.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        9,
        27
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 1"
      ],
      "source": "https://www.minneapolis.org/neighborhoods/south/linden-hills/"
    },
    {
      "id": 4,
      "text": "A historic book, Down at the Lake, chronicles Linden Hills history and is sold at local retailers like Wedge and Settergren’s.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        1
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 2"
      ],
      "source": "https://www.lindenhills.org/lindenhills"
    },
    {
      "id": 5,
      "text": "The Linden Hills History Study Group hosts walking tours, slide shows, and lectures that document the area’s rich past.",
